  <p>
    If you have no reference image or want to design a palette from scratch, use the generator. At the push of a button it creates harmonious color combinations based on color theory, for example monochromatic shades of a base tone. The spacebar delivers a new variant each time until one fits.
  </p>

  <h3>Features at a Glance</h3>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Harmony:</strong> choose the rule by which the colors relate to each other, such as monochromatic.</li>
    <li><strong>Colors:</strong> set the number of fields in the palette.</li>
    <li><strong>Generate with the spacebar:</strong> flip through many suggestions quickly without touching the mouse.</li>
    <li><strong>Lock colors:</strong> if you like a tone, lock it and it survives the next generation.</li>
    <li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> change brightness, contrast, saturation and hue for all colors together or for a single field. Undo, redo and reset are available.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick color:</strong> click a field and fine-tune the tone directly in the color picker.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy:</strong> individual HEX values with one click, or the whole palette via "Copy all".</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="tip-box">
    <p><strong>Combine both parts:</strong> extract colors from a reference photo, take the main tone into the generator and create matching shades for buttons, backgrounds and text there. That turns one image into a complete color scheme.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Typical Use Cases</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Web design:</strong> read color codes from a logo or mood board and use them as CSS variables.</li>
    <li><strong>Presentations and social media:</strong> generate a palette that matches the cover image so graphics and photo work together.</li>
    <li><strong>Brand management:</strong> check which colors actually dominate in existing materials.</li>
    <li><strong>Interior design and crafts:</strong> determine tones from inspiration photos for wall paint or fabrics.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy: Images Stay in Your Browser</h2>

  <p>
    Extraction, image editing and palette generation run entirely locally. No image is uploaded to a server. That makes the tool suitable for unpublished drafts and client material.
  </p>

